WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:03.303
-Our first guest tonight is
a multi-Grammy-Award winning

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.404
musician whose song,
"No Time To Die"

00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:07.673
was recently nominated
for an Academy Award.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:11.010
She is making history as the
youngest artist to headline

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:14.046
both the Glastonbury
and Coachella music festivals

00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:15.582
this year, and is currently on

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:17.450
her "Happier Than Ever"
world tour.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.552
Please welcome to the show,
Billie Eilish, everybody.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.220
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:26.359 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:31.464 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:36.602 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:39.505
-Welcome to the show, Billie!
-Thank you. How you doing?

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:42.008
-I'm fantastic.
I'm so happy to have you here.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.010
And New York has been
so happy to have you here.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.045
You got to play
Madison Square Garden.

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:47.880
-I sure did.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.316
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.785
-I think all of us are in awe

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:56.956
at how much you've accomplished
in your very young life so far.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.425
But I can imagine,
does it still blow your mind,

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.327
when you're in a room like MSG?

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.129
-Yes.
-That's great.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.830
[ Audience awws ]
-Yeah, no, it's great.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.966
I did bawl onstage.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.501
I did.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:10.970
Yeah, it was just really weird.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.338
I have a song during the set

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.407
where it's
all baby footage of me.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.508
[ Audience awws ]

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.610
And I was like,
walking across the stage

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.212
looking at baby me,
looking at the crowd,

00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:21.514
and I bawled.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.815
-Yeah.
-Quite embarrassing.

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:23.849
But what are you gonna do?
-What are you gonna do?

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:25.284
I will say, and again,

00:01:25.284 --> 00:01:26.852
I think the reaction
from this audience

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.020
bears that out --

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.856
I don't think
your audience minds

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:31.090
when you get a little emotional.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.258
-No, they love it.
-Yeah, I think they do, too.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:36.195
[ Cheering ]

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:38.464
And this strikes me as
a relationship you had

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:41.768
with your live audience
even before this pandemic

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.169
that took it away from us,
right?

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.704
You always had a very close
relationship with your audience,

00:01:45.704 --> 00:01:46.973
and one that was very
honest and open.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:48.942
And you always told them
how much they meant to you.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.376
-Yeah.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:56.515
I mean, the fan connection has
been the number one priority

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:57.783
since literally the beginning.

00:01:57.783 --> 00:02:00.086
I wouldn't want to do
any of this without it.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.521
I'm dead serious.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:04.990
There's no reason to do any of
this without the connection.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.258
Like,
literally no reason at all.

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:08.027
-We love you, Billie!

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:11.331
[ Applause ]

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:12.565
-They write a lot of signs.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:13.999
There's a lot of preparation
that goes into

00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:15.168
going to see you live.

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.136
And I think that speaks to
the connection.

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:18.471
-It's ridiculous.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.739
-This makes sense.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.574
I didn't realize this until
I heard you say it.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:25.244
It must be hard to read a sign
while you're singing a song.

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:26.545
-I can't do it.
-Okay.

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:27.680
-I literally can't do it.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.416
I try to, because I want
to read their signs.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:33.252
They work so hard on them.
They color them in and draw.

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:36.922
I -- I -- Yeah.

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:39.325
I'll be like, "Oh, cool sign,"
and I'll read it,

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.293
and then I forget the words,
and it's really bad.

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:42.962
-You wouldn't want to
accidentally

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.029
sing the words on the sign,
sometime.

00:02:44.029 --> 00:02:45.431
-No. No.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:46.832
-This one, you know.

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:48.734
That is somebody who wants, so,

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:51.537
"Sign my body and I will
tattoo it on me."

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:53.606
They want you to sign it
and they would take --

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.641
-That's crazy pressure, man.
Right in the middle of a show?

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:56.842
Please.
-This one, though.

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.177
These are really...

00:02:58.177 --> 00:02:59.379
These are a little bit
harder to read,

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.346
but I've read them earlier.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.515
So this one --
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:05.885
-"Will you pierce my nipples?"

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.053
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:10.389
-Can you imagine if I was like,
"Yeah, let's do it right now."

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:11.925
-"Yeah, let's do it right now."

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.592
And then then this one is even,
this is,

00:03:13.592 --> 00:03:15.627
"Burp into the mic."

00:03:15.627 --> 00:03:18.931
And by the way, I think they
just printed these out.

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:20.032
They didn't even work
that hard on them.

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:21.500
-No, that's true,
but the crazy thing is,

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:25.103
they hold those up literally
for the entire hour and a half.

00:03:25.103 --> 00:03:26.138
They never put them down.

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:27.973
And I'm all like,
"Burp into the mic"?

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:31.577
Like, okay. That's
the statement you want to be...

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:33.145
-Also, it's a very hard thing.
-I love it.

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:36.082
-You want to tell them, like,
"If I do that,

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.583
no one here will understand

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.252
it's 'cause it was on
your weird, little sign."

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.753
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.488
And then sometimes
they collectively,

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.190
like, a large group of them
make signs.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.491
[ Audience awws ]

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:46.893
That's is really nice.
-This makes me cry.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.761
-I mean, look at these faces.
-Yeah.

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:50.563
-They do that.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.933
I think that what they do
is somebody organizes it

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:56.168
and they tell everybody else,
and then they're all like,

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:57.470
"Okay, here's all these signs."

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.039
I'm guessing that they make,
like, a bunch at once

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.241
and then they hand them out
and they're like,

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.808
"For this song,
let's hold them up."

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:03.976
That's what I thought.

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:06.679
It's so cute.
I have cried for that, too.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.748
-And this festival, I mean,

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.350
doing festivals again
must be so exciting,

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.650
and headlining these big...

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.353
How excited are you about
getting back and doing that?

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:15.521
-Oh, my God, so good.

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.790
I did a few in September,
and those were like,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.126
the first back since COVID.

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:21.193
[ Applause ]

00:04:21.193 --> 00:04:22.995
Oh, it feels so good.

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:27.867
-That, especially that time,
obviously another wave came

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:29.401
and made it a little bit
less enthusiastic,

00:04:29.401 --> 00:04:30.736
being out in public,

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:34.473
but that late summer, early fall
was an exceptional time

00:04:34.473 --> 00:04:36.275
to be doing
live performing again.

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:37.877
-Yeah, oh, my God,
we were free.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:39.178
It was great.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:41.347
It was like, a month of like,
"Oh, COVID's gone."

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.049
Nope.

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:45.551
-And then you went
and you did "SNL."

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.253
You hosted "SNL."
-I did.

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:50.723
[ Applause ]

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:53.626
-And like, just got in under the
wire before COVID came back.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.461
-Literally the week before.
-Yeah.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:58.731
-I think the host the week after
you left was omicron.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.199
-Uh-huh. It was.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.867
It was.
-It was omicron.

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:03.736
I have a bunch of questions
about "SNL."

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.137
Stick around,
we will be right back

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:06.873
with more from Billie Eilish.

